      "note": "verified 2026-08-23. WEAKER THAN THE OTHERS AND ACCEPTED KNOWINGLY: this is a document TITLE in the clerk's own news listing, not a sentence. It clears the stamp test by a wide margin -- the posting timestamp beside it is 'April 12, 2023 - 6:25pm', three weeks EARLIER, so May 2 cannot be the CMS date -- and a specimen ballot is headed with the day of the election it is for. Wareham's own return prints only 'May-23' with the day illegible"
